course: dictionary
lesson: 6450
title: Nap: a short sleep, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nap is a short sleep, usually in the day. Nap can also be a verb, so you can nap, or take a nap. «Giraffes sleep very little, in short naps, mostly standing» tells you that a giraffe's sleep is short, and it can happen while the giraffe stands up.
explain: Long sleeps are not naps. «Koalas sleep about 18 to 22 hours a day» means they sleep for most of the day, so that is not a nap. Naps can last minutes or hours, but they are always a sleep you take in the day, and they are shorter than a whole night's sleep.
explain: Nap has a second meaning in the phrase «catch someone napping». It does not mean they are asleep. It means you find them not ready or not paying attention. Use context to decide which meaning fits: is someone sleeping, or are they caught off guard?
fact: A nap is a short sleep, usually in the day.
fact: To nap is to take a short sleep.
fact: «Catch someone napping» means find them not ready or not paying attention.
fact: «Sperm whales nap upright near the surface for short spells, often about a quarter of an hour.»
fact: Babies and small children often nap after lunch, and a «cat nap» or «power nap» is a very short sleep.
exercise: «Sperm whales nap upright near the surface for short spells, often about a quarter of an hour.» About how long is one of their naps? | Several days | A whole year | Eight hours every night | *About a quarter of an hour
exercise: «Galápagos sea lions nap on benches and boats.» In this sentence, what does nap mean? | To swim under the water | *To take a short sleep | To run very fast | To cook food slowly
exercise: «Our goalkeeper was caught napping, and the ball went in.» What does «caught napping» mean here? | Practising a new trick | Fast asleep in bed for the whole night | *Not ready or not paying attention | Lying on the grass, relaxing
test: «Giraffes sleep very little, in short naps, mostly standing.» What does «mostly standing» tell you about giraffe naps? | They never nap at all | They nap under water | They nap lying in the mud | *They often nap while standing up
test: «Koalas sleep about 18 to 22 hours a day.» How much of the day do koalas sleep? | *Most of the day, around 18 to 22 hours | About two hours | Never | Only at night, for an hour
exam: In the phrase «a power nap», what is the power nap most likely? | *A short sleep to get your energy back | A kind of sports game | A very long sleep through the night | A loud noise that wakes you up
